Ignore them, Arthur.  Such spirits are notorious liars.	別理睬牠們，亞瑟。這些靈素以說謊聞名。
We need more silver to appease us.	我們還需要更多銀兩，才能息怒。
Glorious silver!  How pure and perfect it is!  Having silver is better than having a servant!	燦爛的銀啊！何等純淨完美！擁有銀子，勝過擁有一個僕從！
We release you from our service and leave you a gift.	我們解除你為我們服役的義務，並留下一份禮物給你。
The ice here is smooth and unbroken.	這裡的冰面光滑完整，未見裂痕。
Your horse does not want to go in that direction. It must not trust what lies beneath the snow.	你的坐騎不願朝那個方向前進，想必牠不信任積雪底下藏著什麼。
The snow is too deep to go that way.	積雪太深，無法從那邊過去。
You will find the trip even longer and more tiring without your horse, Arthur.	沒有坐騎，這趟路只會顯得更漫長、更疲累，亞瑟。
It is a glittering palace of ice, rising from the center of the lake.	那是一座閃耀的冰宮，聳立在湖心。
You have nearly reached the edge of the lake called Ot Moor.  Through a gap in the bushes, you can catch a glimpse of a palace in the middle of the lake.	你已經接近那座名叫奧特摩爾的湖畔。透過灌木叢間的縫隙，你瞥見湖心有一座宮殿。
Already, there is a touch of warmth returning to this area, but it will take some time for the ice and snow to melt.	這一帶已經漸漸有了一絲暖意回歸，但冰雪要完全消融，還需要一段時日。
That would not be safe in all your heavy gear.	你這身沉重的裝備，這麼做並不安全。
A ridge of ice prevents you from going any further in this direction.	一道冰脊擋住了你，無法再朝這個方向前進。
A huge bank of snow blocks your path.	一大片積雪堵住了你的去路。
You have reached what would normally be the shore of the lake known as Ot Moor.  It is entirely frozen over.	你來到了平時該是奧特摩爾湖岸的地方，如今整片湖面全結了冰。
It will take longer to remove the ice than to make it.  But the thaw begins slowly and the ice is surely more dangerous than it was before.	融去這片冰，要比造出它費上更長的時間。不過解凍已經緩緩展開，這片冰想必也比先前更為危險。
Your horse is too wise to venture onto the ice.	你的坐騎太過聰慧，不會冒險踏上冰面。
Your mule is too intelligent to follow you onto dangerous ice.	你的騾子太過機靈，不會跟著你踏上危險的冰面。
Your horse knows better than to walk upon thin ice.	你的坐騎深知不該在薄冰上行走。
You can observe ice pushed upward into a ridge by the pressure of freezing too quickly.	你可以看出，這道冰脊是急速結凍的壓力將冰面向上推擠而成。
Having reached the towering palace of ice, I must caution you.  In this cold manifestation, the Lady of the Lake may not be the benefactress you have known in the past.	既已抵達這座聳立的冰宮，我必須提醒你：在這副冰冷的化身之中，湖中女神或許已不再是你過去所熟知的那位恩人。
I would guess that the triangular objects on the doors are door handles, though being made of ice do not seem very useful.	我猜門上那些三角形的物件是門把，不過既是冰所製成，似乎派不上什麼用場。
The doors are made of solid ice, the same as the rest of the palace.	這扇門是實心的冰塊所製，與宮殿其餘部分並無二致。
I cannot say what meaning this symbol has.  Perhaps it is a warning, perhaps mere decoration.	我說不出這個符號有何含意，或許是個警示，也或許只是裝飾。
The stairs are made of ice.  Tread carefully.	這階梯以冰築成，小心踩踏。
In the far distance, you glimpse part of the Cotswold Hills.	遠方，你隱約望見科茲沃爾德丘陵的一角。
The Ice Palace is even more beautiful and impressive up close than at a distance.	這座冰宮近看比遠望更加瑰麗懾人。
I would say the two small pyramids of ice are purely decorative.	我想這兩座小冰錐純粹只是裝飾。
This door cannot be opened.	這扇門打不開。
It does not open.  Indeed, there was no reason for you to have returned at all.	它打不開。事實上，你根本沒有理由回到這裡。
Try the other door.	試試另一扇門。
Your arms do not reach that far.	你的手臂搆不到那麼遠。
It is already closed.	它已經關上了。
Gwenhyver is a girl. I am far more than that.	昆海兒不過是個女子，我可遠不止如此。
Remember that finding the Grail is but half the task.  You must also be worthy to possess it.	切記，尋得聖杯不過完成了一半的使命，你還必須配得上擁有它。
Nothing can help, save the return of the object of power which was stolen from me.	唯有歸還那件從我這裡被奪走的力量之物，此外別無他法可以相助。
That which enables me to feel warmth and love, such as the hopeless love I have for Sir Launcelot.	那件事物讓我得以感受溫暖與愛——就像我對蘭斯洛特爵士那段無望的愛戀。
Only the Old Ones had the power to do that.	唯有古代幽靈才有這樣的力量。
Having told you what I know of the Grail, there is but one more boon you can desire of me -- the life of Sir Launcelot.	我已將自己所知關於聖杯之事悉數告訴你，如今你能向我求取的，只剩一項恩惠——蘭斯洛特爵士的性命。
I am loathe to release him.  I offered him my love and he spurned it, for he has given his whole heart to your queen.	我不甘願放他離去。我曾獻上我的愛，他卻棄之不顧，因為他早已將整顆心交給了你的皇后。
If you leave him here, Pendragon, you will be free of him and need never share Gwenhyver's love with him again.	若你把他留在這裡，潘德拉貢，你便能擺脫他，再也不必與他分享昆海兒的愛。
I sense that you possess something that belongs to me.  Give it to me and I will tell you what even Merlin does not know -- where to search for the Grail.	我感覺得到，你身上帶著一件屬於我的東西。將它交還給我，我便告訴你連梅林都不知道的事——該到何處尋找聖杯。
But if you withhold it, you will have neither help nor knowledge from me.	但你若執意扣留不還，我既不會相助，也不會透露半點消息。
He cannot answer you. I have sealed his heartless lips forever, unless you choose to win his freedom.	他無法回答你。我已將他無情的雙唇永遠封住，除非你選擇為他贏得自由。
Blessed be.	願蒙祝福。
That would not help you much.	這對你幫助不大。
Launcelot will never go free, unless you find and return the object of power that was stolen from me.	蘭斯洛特永遠無法獲釋，除非你尋得那件從我這裡被奪走的力量之物，並將它歸還。
No weapon made, not even Excaliber, can shatter this ice formed by my will.	世間沒有一件兵器——即便是聖劍——能夠擊碎這由我意志所凝成的冰。
Money is meaningless to me.	金錢對我毫無意義。
I will not touch it, for it has Gwenhyver's spell upon it.	我不會碰它，因為它身上帶著昆海兒的咒法。
Nay, keep it. I have no use for such a thing.	不必，留著吧。這種東西我用不上。
Aye, that is my heart and contains much of my power. Give it to me and I shall tell you where to search for the Grail.	正是，那便是我的心，蘊藏著我的大半力量。將它交給我，我便告訴你該到何處尋找聖杯。
To free Launcelot will require first my good will. Do not anger me with attempts at bargaining.	要放蘭斯洛特自由，須先贏得我的善意。休得以討價還價來觸怒我。
He is worth far more than that to me.	對我而言，他的價值遠不止於此。
He can accept nothing while frozen in ice.	他被凍在冰中，什麼都無法接受。
I thank you again for the return of the crystal heart, for much of my power is invested within it.	我再次感謝你歸還水晶心，我的大半力量都寄託其中。
If you can return it to me, you will win my help.	你若能將它還給我，便能贏得我的相助。
The ice and cold reflects my mood of late.	這片冰霜寒意，正映照著我近來的心境。
I gave you Excaliber because it is a sword worthy of a king.  Now make sure you are a king worthy of the sword.	我將聖劍賜給你，因為它是一柄配得上君王的劍。如今，你該確保自己是一位配得上這柄劍的君王。
Did you not listen?  Go to Jerusalem, I said.	你沒聽清楚嗎？我說過，前往耶路撒冷。
Bring me the object of power that was stolen from me, and I will tell you where to search.	把那件從我這裡被奪走的力量之物帶來給我，我便告訴你該往何處尋找。
You have but to leave and I will keep Launcelot here, far from Gwenhyver.  I will not harm him, but you will be free of him.	你只需離去，我便會把蘭斯洛特留在此處，遠離昆海兒。我不會傷害他，但你將從此擺脫他。
Launcelot is my prisoner because he has spurned my love and given his heart to your wife, Gwenhyver.  You should thank me, Pendragon, for thus removing your rival for her love.	蘭斯洛特之所以成為我的囚徒，是因為他棄絕了我的愛，把心交給了你的妻子昆海兒。你該感謝我，潘德拉貢，我這是替你除去了情敵。
He did not come here.  Therefore I know nothing of him.	他沒有到過這裡，因此我對他一無所知。
Merlin is your advisor, not I.	梅林才是你的謀士，不是我。
Here stands the Ice Maiden, a cold and unloving manifestation of the Lady of the Lake.  Near her is Sir Launcelot, imprisoned in ice.	此處立著冰霜仙子，那是湖中女神一副冷漠無情的化身。她身旁，蘭斯洛特爵士被囚於冰中。
To reach Jerusalem, you must take ship to the port nearest it in that part of the world.	要抵達耶路撒冷，你得搭船前往那一帶離它最近的港口。
It is dark and cold and uninviting.	那裡陰暗、寒冷，令人不敢靠近。
She looks quite frigid.  But if you are to free Launcelot, you must find a way to win her good will.	她看來十分冷峻。但你若想救出蘭斯洛特，就得設法贏得她的善意。
He is caught in a living death, spellbound in a frozen limbo.	他陷入生死交界的境地，被咒法禁錮在一片冰封的虛無之中。
Everything is ice, formed from the frozen body of the lake by the Ice Maiden's magicks.	這裡的一切皆是冰，是冰霜仙子以法術將湖水凍結而成。
Your good friend and heroic knight, Sir Launcelot, is frozen inside a pillar of ice.	你的摯友、英勇的蘭斯洛特爵士，被凍在一根冰柱之中。
The inside of her palace is lined with stalagmites, stalactites and pillars of ice.	她的宮殿內部，滿佈石筍、鐘乳與冰柱。
These unyielding pillars of ice were formed by the Ice Maiden's will.	這些堅不可摧的冰柱，是冰霜仙子以意志凝成。
This ice pillar no longer holds the frozen body of Launcelot.	這根冰柱裡，已不再封著蘭斯洛特冰封的身軀。
Sir Launcelot is imprisoned in a living death within this pillar of ice.	蘭斯洛特爵士被囚禁在這根冰柱之中，陷入生死交界的境地。
The recesses of the ice palace fade into a shrouded glimmer of frozen shadow.	冰宮深處，隱沒於一片朦朧幽微的冰封暗影之中。
Your lips would stick.	你的雙唇會黏在上面。
She is frigidly disinterested.	她一臉冷漠，毫無興致。
Do you think to threaten ME with the very sword I gave you from my own hand?  Once only will I tolerate this, or you will suffer the fate of Launcelot.	你竟想拿我親手所賜的劍來威脅我？這種事我只容忍一次，否則你將落得與蘭斯洛特相同的下場。
You are a noble man, Pendragon.  But we will see how true is your desire to save Launcelot when you are put to the test.  Follow me.	你是個高尚的人，潘德拉貢。但你救蘭斯洛特的心意究竟有多真切，得等你通過考驗才見分曉。跟我來。
You should have heeded my warning!	你早該聽從我的警告！
As icy fingers seize your spine And coldness numbs your brain You wish instead in battle hot You nobly had been slain.	冰冷的指尖扼住你的脊骨，寒意麻痺了你的神智，你多麼盼望，自己是命喪炙熱的戰場，慷慨捐軀，死得其所。
Alas, your ears are filled with ice You hear not my sad refrain, A frozen statue of despair In winter's hard domain.	可嘆你雙耳已被冰雪封住，再也聽不見我哀傷的吟唱，你將化作一尊絕望的冰像，永立於這嚴酷的寒冬國度。
I shall return you to Camelot!	我將送你返回肯萊特！
I have freed Sir Launcelot and sent him back to Camelot, but your journey goes on.  Farewell, King Arthur, and may you overcome every obstacle with the same wit and courage you have shown here.	我已釋放蘭斯洛特爵士，送他回到肯萊特，但你的旅程仍要繼續。珍重了，亞瑟王，願你此後遭逢的每一道難關，都能以你在此展現的機智與勇氣一一克服。
You may not pass that way, Pendragon, unless I lead you there.	除非由我引路，否則你不得從那條路過去，潘德拉貢。
You may not pass that way.	你不得從那條路過去。
I sense the presence of Merlin.  But I know that which he does not -- where to search for the Grail.  But to win my help, you must find and return an object of power that was stolen from me.	我感應到梅林的存在。但我知曉一件連他都不知道的事——該到何處尋找聖杯。然而要贏得我的相助，你必須尋得一件從我這裡被奪走的力量之物，並將它歸還。
Go, and I will transport you safely across the ice.  Do not return unless you bring it to me!	去吧，我會護送你安然越過這片冰原。除非把它帶來給我，否則休得回來！
Blessed be!  For this greatest of all gifts, I will give you the gift of knowledge in return.	願蒙祝福！為了這份至上的禮物，我將以知識的贈禮回報於你。
To find the Grail, you must take ship to Gaza, then seek Jerusalem.  Somewhere in that city it lies hidden. 	要尋得聖杯，你必須搭船前往加薩，再轉往耶路撒冷。聖杯就隱藏在那座城市之中的某處。 
Once you leave here, I will transport you safely across the ice to continue your search.  But Launcelot I will keep here, for he has spurned my love in favour of your queen. I will not release him, unless you ask it.	你一旦離開此地，我便會護送你安然越過這片冰原，讓你繼續尋覓。但蘭斯洛特，我要留在此處，因為他棄絕了我的愛，選擇了你的皇后。除非你開口求我，否則我不會放他自由。
I can only tell you the name of each flower, if you ask about them.  Beyond that, you must consult your Liber ex Doctrina.	你若問起，我只能告訴你每朵花的名字。除此之外，你得去查閱你的《Liber ex Doctrina》。
It grows from a bed of soil locked in ice.	它從一片封鎖在冰中的土壤裡生長出來。
Clearly, this Miraculous Bush of Flowers is the work of the Lady's sorcery, for it contains many different flowers upon the one bush.	這叢神奇花叢顯然出自女神的法術，因為同一株灌木上竟開著這麼多種花。
Move to where you can best see all the flowers.	移動到能將所有花朵盡收眼底之處。
Very well.  Let the test begin.	很好，考驗開始吧。
Clearly, the bush grows here only by the Ice Maiden's magicks, yet it looks like an ordinary bush in an ordinary patch of soil.	這叢灌木顯然只是憑冰霜仙子的法術才得以在此生長，然而看上去，卻像是尋常土地裡一株尋常的灌木。
These are all the flowers on the Miraculous Bush of Flowers:   almond blossom, anemone, buttercup, chrysanthemum, cornflower, daffodil, forget-me-not, lilly, poppy, and sunflower.	以下是神奇花叢上所有的花：杏花、銀蓮花、毛茛花、菊花、矢車菊、水仙花、勿忘我、百合花、罌粟花，以及向日葵。
In this glittering cave of ice, it is strange and wondrous to see a living thing.  Yet there stands the Miraculous Bush of Flowers.	在這座晶瑩剔透的冰穴之中，能見到一株活物，著實既奇異又奇妙。然而，神奇花叢就佇立在此。
She looks expectant, in a frosty sort of way.	她一臉期待，帶著幾分冷冽的神情。
He is in the pillar of ice and will remain there, unless you pass the Ice Maiden's test and free him.	他被困在冰柱之中，除非你通過冰霜仙子的考驗，否則他將永遠留在那裡。
All but the Bush is ice, formed from the frozen body of the lake by the Ice Maiden's magicks.	除了那叢花，其餘一切皆是冰，是冰霜仙子以法術將湖水凍結而成。
Please consult your Libera ex Doctrina.	請查閱你的《Liber ex Doctrina》。
In every other respect, the bush is quite ordinary.	除此之外，這叢灌木再普通不過。
There are no less than ten flowers upon this bush.	這叢灌木上，開著不下十種花。
First, you must pass my test.	首先，你必須通過我的考驗。
The different flowers fill the air with their mingled fragrances.	各色花朵的香氣交融，瀰漫在空氣之中。
When you are ready for the test, we shall begin.	待你準備妥當，我們便開始考驗。
Come, Pendragon.  My patience is not without limit.  If you will not look at the Bush and take this test, I will send you from here.	來吧，潘德拉貢。我的耐性並非無窮無盡。你若不肯細看這叢花、接受考驗，我便會把你送離此地。
It would seem that your courage has failed you.  Farewell, then.	看來你的勇氣已經棄你而去。那麼，就此別過。
You are worthy of the great legends that will live on in your name.  Come with me.	你當得起那些將以你之名流傳千古的偉大傳說。隨我來。
Do not touch the Miraculous Bush of Flowers.  You may revel in the sight and scent of it, but it is mine alone to touch.	休得碰觸神奇花叢。你可以盡情欣賞它的姿色與香氣，但唯有我能觸碰它。
I warn you most sternly, do not pursue this or I will punish you.	我嚴正警告你，休再堅持，否則我必懲罰你。
To speak the Language of the Flowers means simply to know the special meaning that belongs to each flower, what thought or emotion is associated with it.	所謂通曉花語，不過是知曉每一朵花所蘊含的特殊意涵——它所代表的心思或情感。
Nay, keep it.  I have no use for such a thing.	不必，留著吧。這種東西我用不上。
You are here to free Launcelot.....if you dare.	你來到此地，是為了救出蘭斯洛特……若你敢的話。
It is my Miraculous Bush of Flowers. Go look closely upon the one side that is in bloom.	這是我的神奇花叢。去仔細瞧瞧那一側正在綻放的花朵。
That way is closed to you now, unless you can speak the Language of the Flowers and free Launcelot.	那條路如今已對你封閉，除非你能通曉花語、救出蘭斯洛特。
You will hear me out first.	你得先聽我把話說完。
To free Launcelot, you must speak the Language of the Flowers.  I will pose three riddles.  You must give me the name of the flower that solves each riddle.	要救出蘭斯洛特，你必須通曉花語。我將出三道謎題，你得答出能解開每道謎題的花名。
The Language of the Flowers is the thought or emotion associated with each flower.  If you know this, you may be able to choose correctly.  If you fail even once, you will join Launcelot in a tomb of ice.	花語，便是與每一朵花相繫的心思或情感。你若通曉此道，或許便能選對答案。但凡失手一次，你便要與蘭斯洛特一同困於冰墓之中。
But I will not force this upon you.  Recite the Message of the Rose and I will send you safely away, though Launcelot will not go free.	但我不會強迫你接受考驗。你若誦念玫瑰箴言，我便會送你安然離去，只是蘭斯洛特仍不得自由。
But if you are determined to free your comrade in arms, look closely at the Miraculous Bush of Flowers.  And be warned: once you begin, you may not turn away from your fate.	但你若決意救出這位袍澤，便仔細看清神奇花叢。且要謹記：考驗一旦開始，你便再無法迴避自己的命運。
Use cursor keys or mouse to choose a flower. Press "Enter" or mouse button to answer riddle with the flower you've chosen.	使用方向鍵或滑鼠選擇花朵，按下「Enter」鍵或滑鼠按鈕，以你所選的花朵回答謎題。
Here is the first riddle. Remember, you must choose the flower that best answers it.	這是第一道謎題。切記，你得選出最能解答它的那朵花。
Press F6 to see riddle again	按「F6」鍵可再次查看謎題。
Your wisdom is great. Here is the next riddle.	你的智慧非凡，這是下一道謎題。
Truly you are worthy to be king. The test is ended. Launcelot shall go free.	你確實無愧於王者之名。考驗至此結束，蘭斯洛特將重獲自由。
